<section id=3D"plutosdr-source">
<h3 data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8FPlutoSDR Source<a class=3D"headerlink" href=
=3D"https://antsdr-docs.microphase.cn/en/latest/device_and_usage_manual/ANT=
SDR_E_Series_Module/ANTSDR_E310_Reference_Manual/AntsdrE310_gnurdio.html#pl=
utosdr-source" title=3D"Permalink to this heading">=EF=83=81</a></h3>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8B<strong>RF Bandwidth(MHz)</strong>: Configures=
 RX analog filters: RX TIA LPF and RX BB LPF. <a class=3D"reference externa=
l" href=3D"https://wiki.analog.com/resources/tools-software/linux-drivers/i=
io-transceiver/ad9361#rx_rf_bandwidth_control">Read more</a></p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8B<strong>Sample Rate(MSPS)</strong>: Frequency =
at which the hardware will input/output samples. <a class=3D"reference exte=
rnal" href=3D"https://wiki.analog.com/resources/tools-software/linux-driver=
s/iio-transceiver/ad9361#settingquerying_the_rx_sample_rate">Read more</a><=
/p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8B<strong>LO Frequency(MHz)</strong>: Selects th=
e RX local oscillator frequency. Range 70MHz to 6GHz with 1Hz tuning granul=
arity. <a class=3D"reference external" href=3D"https://wiki.analog.com/reso=
urces/tools-software/linux-drivers/iio-transceiver/ad9361#local_oscillator_=
control_lo">Read more</a></p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8B<strong>Tracking</strong>: <a class=3D"referen=
ce external" href=3D"https://wiki.analog.com/resources/tools-software/linux=
-drivers/iio-transceiver/ad9361#calibration_tracking_controls">Read more</a=
></p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8BQuadrature</p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8BRF DC</p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8BBB DC</p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8B<strong>Manual Gain(dB)</strong>: Controls the=
 RX gain only in Manual Gain Control Mode (MGC). <a class=3D"reference exte=
rnal" href=3D"https://wiki.analog.com/resources/tools-software/linux-driver=
s/iio-transceiver/ad9361#mgc_setting_the_current_gain">Read more</a></p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8B<strong>Gain Mode</strong>: Selects one of the=
 available modes: manual, slow_attack, hybrid and fast_attack. <a class=3D"=
reference external" href=3D"https://wiki.analog.com/resources/tools-softwar=
e/linux-drivers/iio-transceiver/ad9361#gain_control_modes">Read more</a></p=
>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8B<strong>Filter</strong>: Allows a FIR filter c=
onfiguration to be loaded from a file. <a class=3D"reference external" href=
=3D"https://wiki.analog.com/resources/tools-software/linux-drivers/iio-tran=
sceiver/ad9361#digital_fir_filter_controls">Read more</a></p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8B<strong>Filter auto</strong> When enabled load=
s a default filter and thereby enables lower sampling / baseband rates.</p>
<p><img alt=3D"e310" src=3D"https://antsdr-docs.microphase.cn/en/latest/_im=
ages/PlutoSDR_source.png" width=3D"621" height=3D"669"></p>
</section>
<section id=3D"plutosdr-sink">
<h3 data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8FPlutoSDR Sink<a class=3D"headerlink" href=3D"=
https://antsdr-docs.microphase.cn/en/latest/device_and_usage_manual/ANTSDR_=
E_Series_Module/ANTSDR_E310_Reference_Manual/AntsdrE310_gnurdio.html#plutos=
dr-sink" title=3D"Permalink to this heading">=EF=83=81</a></h3>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8B<strong>RF Bandwidth(MHz)</strong>: Configures=
 TX analog filters: TX BB LPF and TX Secondary LPF. <a class=3D"reference e=
xternal" href=3D"https://wiki.analog.com/resources/tools-software/linux-dri=
vers/iio-transceiver/ad9361#tx_rf_bandwidth_control">Read more</a></p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8B<strong>Sample Rate(MSPS)</strong>: Frequency =
at which the hardware will input/output samples. <a class=3D"reference exte=
rnal" href=3D"https://wiki.analog.com/resources/tools-software/linux-driver=
s/iio-transceiver/ad9361#settingquerying_the_tx_sample_rate">Read more</a><=
/p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8B<strong>LO Frequency(MHz)</strong>: Selects th=
e TX local oscillator frequency. Range 70MHz to 6GHz with 1Hz tuning granul=
arity. <a class=3D"reference external" href=3D"https://wiki.analog.com/reso=
urces/tools-software/linux-drivers/iio-transceiver/ad9361#local_oscillator_=
control_lo">Read more</a></p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8B<strong>RF Port Select</strong>: Selects the R=
F port to be used. <a class=3D"reference external" href=3D"https://wiki.ana=
log.com/resources/tools-software/linux-drivers/iio-transceiver/ad9361#rf_po=
rt_selection">Read more</a></p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8B<strong>Attenuation (dB)</strong>: Individuall=
y controls attenuation for TX1 and TX2. The range is from 0 to -89.75 dB in=
 0.25dB steps. <a class=3D"reference external" href=3D"https://wiki.analog.=
com/resources/tools-software/linux-drivers/iio-transceiver/ad9361#tx_attenu=
ation_control">Read more</a></p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8B<strong>Cyclic</strong>: Set to =E2=80=9Ctrue=
=E2=80=9D if the =E2=80=9Ccyclic=E2=80=9D mode is desired. In this case, th=
e first buffer of samples will be repeated on the enabled channels of the F=
MCOMMS-2 until the program is stopped.
The FMCOMMS-2 IIO block will report its processing as complete: the blocks =
connected to the PlutoSDR IIO block won=E2=80=99t execute anymore, but the =
rest of the flow graph will.</p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8B<strong>Filter</strong>: Allows a FIR filter c=
onfiguration to be loaded from a file. <a class=3D"reference external" href=
=3D"https://wiki.analog.com/resources/tools-software/linux-drivers/iio-tran=
sceiver/ad9361#digital_fir_filter_controls">Read more</a></p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8B<strong>Filter auto</strong> When enabled load=
s a default filter and thereby enables lower sampling / baseband rates.</p>
<p><img alt=3D"e310" src=3D"https://antsdr-docs.microphase.cn/en/latest/_im=
ages/plutosdr_sink.png" width=3D"621" height=3D"549"></p>
</section>
</section>
<section id=3D"using-the-fmcomms-blocks">
<h2 data-imt-p=3D"1">5. Using the FMCOMMS Blocks<a class=3D"headerlink" hre=
f=3D"https://antsdr-docs.microphase.cn/en/latest/device_and_usage_manual/AN=
TSDR_E_Series_Module/ANTSDR_E310_Reference_Manual/AntsdrE310_gnurdio.html#u=
sing-the-fmcomms-blocks" title=3D"Permalink to this heading">=EF=83=81</a><=
/h2>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">Before use, you need to use the FMCOMMS firmware. You c=
an find the usage of the FMCOMMS firmware <a class=3D"reference internal" h=
ref=3D"https://antsdr-docs.microphase.cn/en/latest/device_and_usage_manual/=
ANTSDR_E_Series_Module/ANTSDR_E310_Reference_Manual/AntsdrE310_fmcomms.html=
"><span class=3D"doc">here</span></a>.</p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">The FMCOMMS-2 IIO blocks can run over the IP network or=
 USB. By setting the =E2=80=9CIIO context URI=E2=80=9D parameter to the IP =
address of the target board, you can stream samples from/to the remote boar=
d</p>
<p><img alt=3D"e310" src=3D"https://antsdr-docs.microphase.cn/en/latest/_im=
ages/gnuradio_fmcomms.png" width=3D"556" height=3D"602"></p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1"><strong>IIO Context URI</strong>: IP:192.168.1.10</p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1"><strong>Buffer Size</strong>: The size of the internal =
buffer in samples. The IIO module can only input/output one buffer containi=
ng samples at a time</p>
<section id=3D"fmcomms-source">
<h3 data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8FFMCOMMS Source<a class=3D"headerlink" href=3D=
"https://antsdr-docs.microphase.cn/en/latest/device_and_usage_manual/ANTSDR=
_E_Series_Module/ANTSDR_E310_Reference_Manual/AntsdrE310_gnurdio.html#fmcom=
ms-source" title=3D"Permalink to this heading">=EF=83=81</a></h3>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8B<strong>RF Bandwidth(MHz)</strong>: Configures=
 TX analog filters: TX BB LPF and TX Secondary LPF. <a class=3D"reference e=
xternal" href=3D"https://wiki.analog.com/resources/tools-software/linux-dri=
vers/iio-transceiver/ad9361#rx_rf_bandwidth_control">Read more</a></p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8B<strong>Sample Rate(MSPS)</strong>: Frequency =
at which the hardware will input/output samples . <a class=3D"reference ext=
ernal" href=3D"https://wiki.analog.com/resources/tools-software/linux-drive=
rs/iio-transceiver/ad9361#settingquerying_the_rx_sample_rate">Read more</a>=
</p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8B<strong>LO Frequency(MHz)</strong>: Selects th=
e TX local oscillator frequency. Range 70MHz to 6GHz with 1Hz tuning granul=
arity. <a class=3D"reference external" href=3D"https://wiki.analog.com/reso=
urces/tools-software/linux-drivers/iio-transceiver/ad9361#local_oscillator_=
control_lo">Read more</a></p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8B<strong>RF Port Select</strong>: Selects the R=
F port to be used. Can be either any of the inputs on the Rx input mux (in =
single ended or differential) or the Tx monitor input. <a class=3D"referenc=
e external" href=3D"https://wiki.analog.com/resources/tools-software/linux-=
drivers/iio-transceiver/ad9361#rf_port_selection">Read more</a></p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8B<strong>Tracking</strong>: <a class=3D"referen=
ce external" href=3D"https://wiki.analog.com/resources/tools-software/linux=
-drivers/iio-transceiver/ad9361#calibration_tracking_controls">Read more</a=
></p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8BQuadrature</p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8BRF DC</p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8BBB DC</p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8B<strong>Manual Gain(dB)</strong>: Controls the=
 RX gain only in Manual Gain Control Mode (MGC). <a class=3D"reference exte=
rnal" href=3D"https://wiki.analog.com/resources/tools-software/linux-driver=
s/iio-transceiver/ad9361#mgc_setting_the_current_gain">Read more</a></p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8B<strong>Gain Mode(RX1, RX2)</strong>: Selects =
one of the available modes: manual, slow_attack, hybrid and fast_attack. <a=
 class=3D"reference external" href=3D"https://wiki.analog.com/resources/too=
ls-software/linux-drivers/iio-transceiver/ad9361#gain_control_modes">Read m=
ore</a></p>
<p><img alt=3D"e310" src=3D"https://antsdr-docs.microphase.cn/en/latest/_im=
ages/fmcomms_sink.png" width=3D"599" height=3D"548"></p>
</section>
<section id=3D"fmcomms-sink">
<h3 data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8FFMCOMMS Sink<a class=3D"headerlink" href=3D"h=
ttps://antsdr-docs.microphase.cn/en/latest/device_and_usage_manual/ANTSDR_E=
_Series_Module/ANTSDR_E310_Reference_Manual/AntsdrE310_gnurdio.html#fmcomms=
-sink" title=3D"Permalink to this heading">=EF=83=81</a></h3>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8B<strong>RF Bandwidth(MHz)</strong>: Configures=
 TX analog filters: TX BB LPF and TX Secondary LPF. <a class=3D"reference e=
xternal" href=3D"https://wiki.analog.com/resources/tools-software/linux-dri=
vers/iio-transceiver/ad9361#rx_rf_bandwidth_control">Read more</a></p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8B<strong>Sample Rate(MSPS)</strong>: Frequency =
at which the hardware will input/output samples . <a class=3D"reference ext=
ernal" href=3D"https://wiki.analog.com/resources/tools-software/linux-drive=
rs/iio-transceiver/ad9361#settingquerying_the_rx_sample_rate">Read more</a>=
</p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8B<strong>LO Frequency(MHz)</strong>: Selects th=
e TX local oscillator frequency. Range 70MHz to 6GHz with 1Hz tuning granul=
arity. <a class=3D"reference external" href=3D"https://wiki.analog.com/reso=
urces/tools-software/linux-drivers/iio-transceiver/ad9361#local_oscillator_=
control_lo">Read more</a></p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8B<strong>RF Port Select</strong>: Selects the R=
F port to be used. Can be either any of the inputs on the Rx input mux (in =
single ended or differential) or the Tx monitor input. <a class=3D"referenc=
e external" href=3D"https://wiki.analog.com/resources/tools-software/linux-=
drivers/iio-transceiver/ad9361#rf_port_selection">Read more</a></p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1"><strong>Attenuation(RX1, RX2)(dB)</strong>: Individuall=
y controls attenuation for TX1 and TX2. The range is from 0 to -89.75 dB in=
 0.25dB steps. <a class=3D"reference external" href=3D"https://wiki.analog.=
com/resources/tools-software/linux-drivers/iio-transceiver/ad9361#tx_attenu=
ation_control">Read more</a></p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8B<strong>Cyclic</strong>: Set to =E2=80=9Ctrue=
=E2=80=9D if the =E2=80=9Ccyclic=E2=80=9D mode is desired. In this case, th=
e first buffer of samples will be repeated on the enabled
channels of the FMCOMMS-2 until the program is stopped.</p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">The FMCOMMS-2 IIO block will report its processing as c=
omplete: the blocks connected to the FMCOMMS-2 IIO block won=E2=80=99t exec=
ute anymore, but the rest of the flow graph will.</p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8B<strong>TX1/TX2</strong> Enabled: Enables the =
transmit data path</p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8B<strong>Filter</strong>: Allows a FIR filter c=
onfiguration to be loaded from a file. <a class=3D"reference external" href=
=3D"https://wiki.analog.com/resources/tools-software/linux-drivers/iio-tran=
sceiver/ad9361#digital_fir_filter_controls">Read more</a></p>
<p data-imt-p=3D"1">=E2=97=8B<strong>Filter auto</strong> When enabled, a d=
efault filter is loaded, enabling lower sampling and baseband rates.
<img alt=3D"e310" src=3D"https://antsdr-docs.microphase.cn/en/latest/_image=
s/fmcomms_source.png" width=3D"621" height=3D"761"></p>
</section>
</section>
</section>


